        "additional_instructions": "NORTH/REAR VIEW ONLY of the SAME male character. First input is the exact standing rear pose; next eight are the exact approved rear walk poses in order. Fit ONLY the approved brown leather work boots from the same-body South standing reference, seen FROM BEHIND. Reference is a FRONT design/material guide: do not rotate the bodies or draw front-facing lace panels on their heels. Practical low ankle-height work boots, warm medium-dark brown leather, dark charcoal rubber soles, simple back seam and small pull tab, restrained heel shading. No bright badges, gold, orange, spurs or fashion heels. Full boot shafts, because accepted jeans will draw OVER the tops as a separate layer. Cover each original ankle and bare foot at its exact native position; preserve EACH foot's actual lowest opaque row, ground contact and lift in every pose. Keep central leg gap. No enlarged stance, dragging soles, floating boots, new gait or shifted/scaled anatomy. Stable coherent leather shading across the sequence. No jeans, jacket, hair or other gear. Keep original head, hands, underwear, limbs and 48x64 canvas with pivot (24,58). Only footwear pixels will be extracted over unchanged original bodies; all generated anatomy is discarded."
